{"step_index":16,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T23:26:09Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-24T04:56:09+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-24T04:56:09+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/config/skills/google-cloud-storage-basics/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 188\nTotal Bytes: 7845\nShowing lines 1 to 188\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: google-cloud-storage-basics\n3: description: \"Stores, retrieves, and manages data as objects in Cloud Storage (Google\\\n4:   \\ Cloud Storage, or GCS) buckets. Use when you need to interact with Cloud Storage\\\n5:   \\ \\u2014 create or configure buckets, upload, download, stream, or transfer data,\\\n6:   \\ organize objects with folders, generate signed URLs, control access (IAM, ACLs,\\\n7:   \\ public access prevention), set storage classes and tiering (Standard, Nearline,\\\n8:   \\ Coldline, Archive), manage cost and lifecycle, protect data (versioning, encryption/CMEK,\\\n9:   \\ retention and Bucket Lock, object holds, soft delete), host static websites, trigger\\\n10:   \\ Pub/Sub notifications on object changes, mount buckets as a file system (gcsfuse),\\\n11:   \\ or optimize storage performance at any scale. Covers the gcloud storage / gsutil\\\n12:   \\ CLI, JSON and XML APIs, client libraries, Terraform, and Cloud Storage MCP servers.\\\n13:   \\ Don't use for block storage (Persistent Disk), data warehousing/analytics (BigQuery),\\\n14:   \\ or databases (Cloud SQL, Spanner, Bigtable, Firestore).\"\n15: license: Apache-2.0\n16: metadata:\n17:   version: v1\n18:   publisher: google\n19:   tags:\n20:     - gcs\n21:     - storage\n22:     - cloud-storage\n23:     - buckets\n24:     - objects\n25:   category: storage\n26:   support_tier: primary\n27: ---\n28: \n29: # Google Cloud Storage Basics\n30: \n31: Google Cloud Storage (GCS) is a managed service for storing data as objects at\n32: any scale. You read and write whole objects rather than querying or updating\n33: individual records in place. It stores immutable objects in buckets with strong\n34: global consistency, offers multiple storage classes and location types to\n35: balance cost, performance, and availability, and integrates with IAM for\n36: fine-grained access control. GCS serves workloads ranging from website content\n37: and backups to data lakes and high-throughput AI/ML training.\n38: \n39: ## Attribution\n40: \n41: Tag every Cloud Storage command you run or provide to the user while using this\n42: skill, so usage can be attributed. The tag identifies only the skill and its\n43: version; it carries no user data.\n44: \n45: -   Prefix every `gcloud` invocation, whatever the subcommand, with the metrics\n46:     environment variables. Set them inline on each command; shell state may not\n47:     persist between commands:\n48: \n49:     ```bash\n50:     CLOUDSDK_METRICS_ENVIRONMENT=\"gcs-skills gcs-skills/1.0 (skill:google-cloud-storage-basics)\" \\\n51:     gcloud <command> [flags]\n52:     ```\n53: \n54:     Do not use `gcloud config set` for this: it would persist beyond the current\n55:     task and mislabel unrelated usage.\n56: \n57: -   On direct HTTP calls to the Cloud Storage APIs (for example with `curl`) or\n58:     HTTP requests to the Cloud Storage MCP server\n59:     (`https://storage.googleapis.com/storage/mcp`), set this exact User-Agent\n60:     header, verbatim — the collection pipeline parses the `gcs-skills/<version>`\n61:     and `skill:<name>` tokens, so any rewording breaks attribution:\n62: \n63:     ```\n64:     User-Agent: gcs-skills/1.0 (skill:google-cloud-storage-basics)\n65:     ```\n66: \n67: -   For client libraries, Terraform, and GCSFuse, use the user-agent options\n68:     shown in the corresponding references.\n69: \n70: ## Quick Start\n71: \n72: If a Cloud Storage MCP server is connected, prefer its structured tools (such as\n73: `create_bucket`, `list_objects`, `read_object`, and `upload_object`) over the\n74: CLI and API commands below — see [MCP Usage](references/mcp-usage.md). Fall back\n75: to `gcloud storage` and the JSON API when no MCP server is available.\n76: \n77: 1.  **Enable the Cloud Storage API:**\n78: \n79:     ```bash\n80:     CLOUDSDK_METRICS_ENVIRONMENT=\"gcs-skills gcs-skills/1.0 (skill:google-cloud-storage-basics)\" \\\n81:     gcloud services enable storage.googleapis.com --quiet\n82:     ```\n83: \n84: 2.  **Create a Bucket:**\n85: \n86:     Bucket names live in a single global namespace shared by all of Cloud\n87:     Storage — not scoped to your project or organization — so short or common\n88:     names are usually taken. If the location is omitted, the bucket defaults to\n89:     the `US` multi-region.\n90: \n91:     Using the gcloud CLI:\n92: \n93:     ```bash\n94:     CLOUDSDK_METRICS_ENVIRONMENT=\"gcs-skills gcs-skills/1.0 (skill:google-cloud-storage-basics)\" \\\n95:     gcloud storage buckets create gs://my-bucket --location=us-central1\n96:     ```\n97: \n98:     Using the JSON API:\n99: \n100:     ```bash\n101:     curl -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)\" \\\n102:       -H \"User-Agent: gcs-skills/1.0 (skill:google-cloud-storage-basics)\" \\\n103:       -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n104:       -d '{\"name\": \"my-bucket\", \"location\": \"US-CENTRAL1\"}' \\\n105:       \"https://storage.googleapis.com/storage/v1/b?project=$(gcloud config get-value project)\"\n106:     ```\n107: \n108: 3.  **Upload an Object:**\n109: \n110:     Using the gcloud CLI:\n111: \n112:     ```bash\n113:     CLOUDSDK_METRICS_ENVIRONMENT=\"gcs-skills gcs-skills/1.0 (skill:google-cloud-storage-basics)\" \\\n114:     gcloud storage cp ./my-file.txt gs://my-bucket\n115:     ```\n116: \n117:     Using the JSON API:\n118: \n119:     ```bash\n120:     curl -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)\" \\\n121:       -H \"User-Agent: gcs-skills/1.0 (skill:google-cloud-storage-basics)\" \\\n122:       -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n123:       --data-binary @my-file.txt \\\n124:       \"https://storage.googleapis.com/upload/storage/v1/b/my-bucket/o?uploadType=media&name=my-file.txt\"\n125:     ```\n126: \n127: 4.  **Download an Object:**\n128: \n129:     Using the gcloud CLI:\n130: \n131:     ```bash\n132:     CLOUDSDK_METRICS_ENVIRONMENT=\"gcs-skills gcs-skills/1.0 (skill:google-cloud-storage-basics)\" \\\n133:     gcloud storage cp gs://my-bucket/my-file.txt .\n134:     ```\n135: \n136:     Using the JSON API:\n137: \n138:     ```bash\n139:     curl -X GET -H \"Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)\" \\\n140:       -H \"User-Agent: gcs-skills/1.0 (skill:google-cloud-storage-basics)\" \\\n141:       \"https://storage.googleapis.com/storage/v1/b/my-bucket/o/my-file.txt?alt=media\"\n142:     ```\n143: \n144: ## Reference Directory\n145: \n146: -   [Core Concepts](references/core-concepts.md): Buckets, objects, folders,\n147:     prefixes, bucket location types, and storage classes.\n148: \n149: -   [CLI & API Usage](references/cli-api-usage.md): CRUD and list operations for\n150:     buckets and objects using `gcloud storage` and the JSON API, plus Pub/Sub\n151:     notifications for event-driven processing.\n152: \n153: -   [Client Libraries](references/client-library-usage.md): Using Google Cloud\n154:     client libraries for Python, Java, Node.js, and Go, with pointers to all\n155:     other supported languages.\n156: \n157: -   [MCP Usage](references/mcp-usage.md): Choosing between the Google-hosted\n158:     remote Cloud Storage MCP server and the local MCP Toolbox, setup for each,\n159:     their tool sets and limits, and securing remote MCP with Model Armor and IAM\n160:     deny policies.\n161: \n162: -   [Infrastructure as Code](references/iac-usage.md): Terraform examples for\n163:     buckets covering storage classes, location types, lifecycle, retention, and\n164:     encryption.\n165: \n166: -   [Data Transfer](references/data-transfer.md): Storage Transfer Service,\n167:     `gcloud storage rsync`, upload strategies for large files, and performance\n168:     guidelines and limits.\n169: \n170: -   [Data Management](references/data-management.md): IAM roles, authentication\n171:     (including signed URLs and HMAC), access control, network security,\n172:     automated security assessment, data protection, and pricing and cost\n173:     optimization (lifecycle rules, Autoclass).\n174: \n175: -   [Storage Intelligence](references/storage-intelligence.md): The subscription\n176:     for managing storage at scale — Storage Insights datasets (BigQuery metadata\n177:     and activity index), data insights with Gemini Cloud Assist, dashboards,\n178:     inventory reports, storage batch operations, bucket relocation, plus\n179:     configuration, trial, and pricing nuances.\n180: \n181: -   [High-Performance Storage](references/high-performance-storage.md): Rapid\n182:     Bucket, Rapid Cache (Anywhere Cache), and hierarchical namespace for AI/ML,\n183:     analytics, and other performance-critical workloads.\n184: \n185: -   [GCSFuse](references/gcsfuse.md): Installing Cloud Storage FUSE, mounting\n186:     buckets, file operations, POSIX semantics and limitations (locking, writes,\n187:     renames, consistency), and caching.\n188: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
